## 🛠️ LUMOS DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

### **AI Testing Commands (Always Available)**

#### **Core Lumos Commands**
```bash
lumos analyze <error>           # AI-powered error analysis with multi-provider consensus
lumos validate [testPath]       # Test quality assessment with coverage analysis
lumos debug [options]          # Visual debugging with Playwright automation
lumos research <query>         # Community solution mining from Stack Overflow/GitHub
lumos watch [directory]        # Real-time file monitoring with auto-analysis
lumos init [options]           # Initialize Lumos configuration with AI provider setup
lumos cache clear              # Clear pattern recognition cache
lumos cache stats              # Display cache statistics and learning metrics
```

#### **Development Commands**
```bash
npm run dev                    # Development mode with tsx watch
npm run dev:debug              # Debug mode with Node.js inspector
npm run build                  # TypeScript compilation + executable permissions
npm run build:watch            # Watch mode TypeScript compilation
npm test                       # Vitest test suite with coverage
npm run test:watch             # Interactive test development
npm run test:coverage          # Comprehensive coverage reporting
npm run test:ui                # Vitest UI for interactive testing
npm run test:playwright        # End-to-end Playwright testing
npm run test:e2e               # Chromium-specific E2E tests
npm run lint                   # ESLint with TypeScript strict rules
npm run lint:fix               # Auto-fix linting issues
npm run typecheck              # TypeScript strict mode validation
npm run typecheck:watch        # Watch mode type checking
```

#### **Documentation & Release Commands**
```bash
npm run docs:serve             # MkDocs local development server
npm run docs:build             # Build static documentation site
npm run docs:deploy            # Deploy to GitHub Pages
npm run docs:generate          # Generate TypeDoc API documentation
npm run format                 # Prettier code formatting
npm run format:check           # Check formatting compliance
npm run release:dry            # Dry run semantic release
```

