## 🔧 COMPLETE AI TESTING SDLC

### **Phase 1: Setup & Configuration**
```bash
# 1. Clone and setup Lumos
git clone https://github.com/dakshana-jayakumar/lumos.git
cd lumos
npm install

# 2. Environment setup for AI providers
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your API keys:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key
# GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY=your_google_key

# 3. Initialize Lumos configuration
lumos init --preset enterprise --ai-providers openai,anthropic
```

### **Phase 2: Development & Testing**
```bash
# 1. Start development environment
npm run dev                    # tsx watch mode for rapid development

# 2. Run comprehensive test suite
npm run test:watch            # Unit tests with Vitest in watch mode
npm run test:playwright       # E2E testing with Playwright automation
npm run test:coverage         # Generate coverage reports

# 3. Quality assurance pipeline
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build
```

### **Phase 3: AI Testing Intelligence Workflows**
```bash
# 1. Error analysis workflow
lumos analyze "TypeError: Cannot read property 'click' of null" \
  --context src/components/ \
  --research \
  --fix-suggestions \
  --confidence 0.8

# 2. Test validation and quality assessment
lumos validate tests/ \
  --coverage \
  --flaky-detection \
  --best-practices \
  --output validation-report.html

# 3. Visual debugging for UI test failures
lumos debug \
  --screenshot error-screenshot.png \
  --dom-state dom-dump.html \
  --network-logs network.har \
  --auto-analyze
```

### **Phase 4: Continuous Integration**
```bash
# 1. Pre-commit validation
npm run lint:staged           # Lint staged files only
npm run typecheck             # Strict TypeScript validation

# 2. CI pipeline commands
npm run test:coverage         # Generate coverage for CI
npm run test:playwright       # E2E testing in CI environment
npm run benchmark             # Performance benchmarking

# 3. Documentation deployment
npm run docs:build && npm run docs:deploy  # Deploy docs to GitHub Pages
```

